  "explanation": "The ranking prioritizes patches that target the frame/pause logic and output storage controls around the first mismatch window (cycles 8-16). The top candidates substitute frame-related signals into store enables (patch_28182ef789d2, patch_c05548e3a8e5) and add temp register reset (patch_489a75ddcd7b), addressing the m_axis_tdata/m_axis_tlast/m_axis_tuser divergence at cycles 13-16. Mid-ranked patches gate the frame-advance condition on rate_by_frame (patch_6f8298dc7749) and qualify output-store enables with valid/ready/reset signals (patch_d09dad2fed72, patch_413743f5dfd2, patch_b857ef3ece44), which influence the pause/ready behavior seen at cycles 12-15. The last patch gates the pause condition on rate_by_frame (patch_fd49deeec05e). Patches directly modifying s_axis_tready_reg or m_axis_tvalid_reg initial values were deprioritized because they affect earlier cycles without explaining the frame-correlated data/last/user errors."
